[Mount Rokkō](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/028h4p), [Awaji Island](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/021927), and the [Tajima Highlands](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/03c89pr) are the three best locations in Hyogo Prefecture to anchor a military force, each offering distinct tactical advantages depending on your story’s survival setup. [1] 
Hyogo is uniquely positioned because it is the only prefecture that stretches entirely across Japan's main island, touching both the Seto Inland Sea in the south and the Sea of Japan in the north. This geographic diversity provides compelling options for a fictional base. [2, 3, 4] 
------------------------------
## 1. [Mount Rokkō](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/028h4p) (The Mountain Fortress)

* Strategic Type: Fortified Command Center / Air & Artillery Support.
* Tactical Advantage: [Mount Rokkō](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/028h4p) rises directly behind the dense urban coastline of Kobe.
* Story Value: If your setting involves a "high mutation" wasteland in the massive Osaka/Kobe metropolitan area, [Mount Rokkō](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/028h4p) acts as an untouchable citadel looking down on the chaos. It has a natural 931-meter elevation advantage, clear lines of sight across the entire Osaka Bay, and steep, easily defensible ridgelines. A military force here could hold out indefinitely using high-altitude advantages and drone or helicopter deployments. [1] 

## 2. [Awaji Island](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/021927) (The Controlled Isolation Zone)

* Strategic Type: Naval Base / Large-Scale Defensive Settlement.
* Tactical Advantage: A massive island at the mouth of Osaka Bay.
* Story Value: This is perfect for a "low mutation" safe zone. Because it is separated from the mainland, a military faction could easily fortify and seal off the two entry points: the Akashi Kaikyō Bridge in the north and the Ōnaruto Bridge in the south. It features flat land for agriculture to feed a military regime, a long coastline to deploy a naval fleet, and absolute control over maritime shipping lanes moving into central Japan. [1] 

## 3. [Tajima Highlands](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/03c89pr) / [Toyooka](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/01wnkj) (The Hidden Outpost)

* Strategic Type: Guerrilla Base / Deep Wilderness Cache.
* Tactical Advantage: Dense, rugged mountains facing the Sea of Japan in northern Hyogo.
* Story Value: If your military force is small, renegade, or hiding from a larger threat, the northern Tajima region (near [Toyooka](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/01wnkj) or [Yabu](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=/m/0636fg)) provides brutal, heavily forested terrain. The harsh winter snows and deeply carved valleys make it nearly impossible for an outside force to root them out, allowing them to run covert cross-border operations into neighboring Kyoto or Tottori prefectures. [2, 5] 

